.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man1/kbd_mode.1, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt KBD_MODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kbd_mode
.Nd report or set the console keyboard mode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a | u | k | s | d
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl C Ar console
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
with no mode option reports the keyboard mode.
It uses the console on standard input unless
.Fl C
names a device.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Select translated 8-bit input, K_XLATE.
.It Fl u
Select translated UTF-8 input, K_UNICODE.
.It Fl k
Select keycodes, K_MEDIUMRAW.
.It Fl s
Select scan codes, K_RAW.
.It Fl d
Disable console keyboard input, K_OFF.
.It Fl f
Force a change to or from a raw mode.
.It Fl C Ar console
Use this console device.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Restore translated input after a program left the console in raw mode:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kbd_mode -f -u -C /dev/console
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loadkeys 1 ,
.Xr showkey 1
